(6786970, 1018628, 100831, '<td valign="top">brilliant peek through with excellent light. She looks happy though, hard to believe she''s a madame in a sense of the word.</td>', 'brilliant peek through with excellent light. She looks happy though, hard to believe she''s a madame in a sense of the word.', '2012-06-06 00:11:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6786990, 1018630, 10785, '<td valign="top">You did a good job with the light on the shot. There is a nice rim lighting on the head and shoulders, which tells me the shot was lit from behind the subject. So you also did a good job getting the front of the subject lit. Since the main light (sky) was in front of you there was a good chance of the background being blown or the front of the statue being in shadow and dark.<br/> <br/>Some things to improve upon, try to keep the shot a little cleaner looking by limiting the distracting background. One way would be to use a wider aperture to cause blur, the other way would be to shoot from above to include only the green grass, or shoot from belw to get more sky. Also, centering the statue in the frame left to right would have heled a little.<br/> <br/>Hope this feedback was helpful and not too basic.</td>', 'You did a good job with the light on the shot. There is a nice rim lighting on the head and shoulders, which tells me the shot was lit from behind the subject. So you also did a good job getting the front of the subject lit. Since the main light (sky) was in front of you there was a good chance of the background being blown or the front of the statue being in shadow and dark. Some things to improve upon, try to keep the shot a little cleaner looking by limiting the distracting background. One way would be to use a wider aperture to cause blur, the other way would be to shoot from above to include only the green grass, or shoot from belw to get more sky. Also, centering the statue in the frame left to right would have heled a little. Hope this feedback was helpful and not too basic.', '2012-06-06 00:39:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6786993, 1018287, 10785, '<td valign="top">The detail on this shot just draws me right in... It''s like shot in HD! I just love how you captured the soft light and let it flow through the opening in the trees right through the shot?</td>', 'The detail on this shot just draws me right in... It''s like shot in HD! I just love how you captured the soft light and let it flow through the opening in the trees right through the shot?', '2012-06-06 00:42:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6786998, 1018681, 10785, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot for the family album. Great emotion. I don''t really think anything was gained using a square crop. My eye travels from the people to the end of the fishing rod, which is cut off.  This would be fine cropped at a 2:3 ratio if using a crop frame sensor. Also, watch the position of the people in the frame... The woman''s foot is partially chopped off and I think I wold be better to include it.</td>', 'Lovely shot for the family album. Great emotion. I don''t really think anything was gained using a square crop. My eye travels from the people to the end of the fishing rod, which is cut off.  This would be fine cropped at a 2:3 ratio if using a crop frame sensor. Also, watch the position of the people in the frame... The woman''s foot is partially chopped off and I think I wold be better to include it.', '2012-06-06 00:50:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6786999, 1018105, 10785, '<td valign="top">Why cut this off with that frame. The whole shot radiates outward because of the lines of the web, then I feel like I get chopped off at the frame. Stunning shot, horrible use of frame.</td>', 'Why cut this off with that frame. The whole shot radiates outward because of the lines of the web, then I feel like I get chopped off at the frame. Stunning shot, horrible use of frame.', '2012-06-06 00:53:20.000000', NULL, 1),
