(6790058, 1016236, 54778, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jomari:</b></div><hr/><i> Great viewpoint here. Are you privy to this scene on an ongoing basis? All those hungry little beaks! I wonder if she''ll stuff the moth into one or if she''ll dismember it? Or does she have to eat it herself and regurgitate? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I haven''t had the opportunity to really see them in action because the parents would not feed the children when I had a clear view. They would go in and go out really swiftly and I assumed they were regurgitating but they always took solid moths with them so maybe they crushed them intead? I think this is red vented bulbul so I''ll see if that could tell something about their eating habits.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-06-08 02:25:25.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by jomari: Great viewpoint here. Are you privy to this scene on an ongoing basis? All those hungry little beaks! I wonder if she''ll stuff the moth into one or if she''ll dismember it? Or does she have to eat it herself and regurgitate?  I haven''t had the opportunity to really see them in action because the parents would not feed the children when I had a clear view. They would go in and go out really swiftly and I assumed they were regurgitating but they always took solid moths with them so maybe they crushed them intead? I think this is red vented bulbul so I''ll see if that could tell something about their eating habits.', '2012-06-08 03:22:48.000000', '2012-06-08 03:25:25.000000', 0),
