(6790599, 1018306, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> "Tuscany meets the water on the western side too (Tyrrhenian Sea/Ligurian Sea)."<br/> <br/>Isn''t that the only side it meets the water on? I spent some time on this Western coast, in Pisa and some town named after a Saint. It''s beautiful, of course. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Correct.  Poor choice of words by me.  I guess I meant to say that Tuscany not only has all the things that it is known for but also meets the water too.  Thanks for hanging this in your art gallery! :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-06-08 13:31:46.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: "Tuscany meets the water on the western side too (Tyrrhenian Sea/Ligurian Sea)." Isn''t that the only side it meets the water on? I spent some time on this Western coast, in Pisa and some town named after a Saint. It''s beautiful, of course.   Correct.  Poor choice of words by me.  I guess I meant to say that Tuscany not only has all the things that it is known for but also meets the water too.  Thanks for hanging this in your art gallery! :)', '2012-06-08 14:31:18.000000', '2012-06-08 14:31:46.000000', 0),
